  "step_2": "The decision reason evaluates skewness and prefers the more right-skewed lottery. Since neither Lottery A nor Lottery B is right-skewed (Lottery A is left-skewed, Lottery B is symmetric with no tail), there is no preference according to the reason. Thus, the reason is indifferent between the lotteries.",
  "final_answer": "INDIFFERENT"
}

